Thanks for all the diagnostics.

 > But now I get a runtime error with Wawro's stuff in the current svn
 > directory

Turns out you just need "data_file" (and not
to use "~/" in your paths, which is why I
didn't find it at first).

 > Also, when compiling I get some warnings, most of which look harmless.

If they're warnings, they're probably harmless.

Clang seems to get confused by unused symbols.
We haven't figured out a good way to suppress them
cross-platform.

I don't know what's up with the C++0x11 warnings now.
I know Daniel's been tweaking the makefile for
generality of targets and specificity of platforms.
I'm guessing a flag got misplaced.

- Bob

