caused) at this point because that is neither the model we are trying
to estimate, nor the model that WinBUGS does estimate, nor the model
that BUGS recommends estimating. For the model vanilla_ice is trying
to replicate:

www.mrc-bsu.cam.ac.uk/bugs/documentation/exampVol2/node15.html <http://www.mrc-bsu.cam.ac.uk/bugs/documentation/exampVol2/node15.html>

speaks to Matt's point somewhat. They work out the full-conditional
distribution of tau and stick into the BUGS model. Apparently, BUGS
has some precedence heuristics where if you do that it adjusts its
behavior accordingly. I am guessing that part of the problem we are
getting with vanilla_ice in Stan is that we shouldn't just be
literally translating that BUGS code into Stan code because the bit
about the FCD of tau is out of place in Stan. If I am correct, then we
should just put a vague prior on tau and roll?

Ben

