To reemphasize what Bob just said, the issue isn't just a question of vanilla versus pineapple. It's that there is no way in Stan to specify a distribution in terms of its conditionals. None. You have to specify the full joint via some kind of factorization that respects the chain rule of probability. So it's not a subtle question of the way that pineapple_ice or vanilla_ice handles tau, it's that there simply is no correct way to specify the ice model this way in Stan.

