Ergh. The part of my thinking that I neglected to actually write down
was that we should write in the .stan file a joint prior on the betas
that corresponds to that implied by WinBUGS's Conditional
AutoRegressive prior. Then put a vague prior on tau, then those priors
and the likelihood should yield a posterior that Stan can sample from.
I think (if I am reading the original article correctly) that the
joint prior on the betas is just a multivariate normal with a very
particular covariance matrix (even more particular than the usual AR1
covariance matrix). So, this seems to be more of an issue of (Win)BUGS
making things more complicated than they need to be because (Win)BUGS
is not that good with joint priors over multivariate parameters?

